      "writtenOn": "2025-11-20T13:31:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: I think it would be clearer to have an explicit if in the caller. For example at [1] we\u0027d have:\n\n```\n    if (device-\u003eHasFeature(Feature::Float32Blendable)) {\n        AddCaps({wgpu::TextureFormat::R32Float, wgpu::TextureFormat::RG32Float,\n             wgpu::TextureFormat::RGBA32Float},\n            Cap::Blendable);\n    }\n```\n\nIt\u0027d also remove the need to have comment that just copy the name of the feature, since it would clearly be in the `if()`.\n\nI realize that this automatically takes care of annotating why formats are not supported, but IMHO it would be just as good to be explicit about the unsupported reason.",
      "revId": "64c444471125f787add28da03178e863fad38481",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
